Project: PKNS AMP Hub, a pitch prototype (React 18 + Vite, plain CSS, no backend). All data is dummy and generated in the browser. AMP means Advertising, Marketing and Promotion.

This is not a leasing CRM. Do not add unit grids, asking rent, lease expiry, occupancy as a product KPI, or a leasing pipeline. The only occupancy figure is the read-only RentX snapshot on an asset, marked sample data.

Build instructions
- README.md is how to run it. `npm run verify` and `npm run verify:consistency` check the AMP acceptance rules in scripts/verify.mjs. They must print ALL CHECKS PASSED.
- The previous leasing brief in BUILD_PROMPT.md is retired.

Source of truth
- src/data/config.js holds asset names (each marked VERIFY NAME), operators, activation types and volumes. src/data/generate.js builds the set with seed 20261028. src/data/metrics.js holds the formulas.

Hard rules
- Never hard-code a figure in a screen. Read from the store and compute with src/data/metrics.js and src/data/selectors.js.
- Live session changes live in src/store.jsx and must flow through the selectors so every screen updates together.
- After any change to config.js, generate.js or metrics.js run `npm run verify`.
- No scores, health ratings, traffic-light colours, AI judgements or recommendation text. Show raw numbers with sort and filter. Series colours are neutral.
- Every table: sortable columns, numbers right-aligned, Export CSV, pagination 25/50/100, empty state. Totals where a total makes sense.
- Use format.js helpers. Currency is `RM 12,450`. Chart axes may use rmAxis.
- Keep the Demo data and Prototype tags visible. Do not put a vendor name in the interface. UI English. Public forms bilingual. Social captions stay in Bahasa Malaysia as written in config.js.
- Personal data is masked until reveal. Consented contact export is AMP Manager only and states how many rows were excluded.
- Navigation uses hash routes via go() from src/router.js. Hide nav items the role cannot access.
- Do not add a new UI framework or TypeScript toolchain. Do not add runtime libraries beyond the ones already in package.json.
